WEBVTT

00:21:58.692 --> 00:22:01.271
and I got a commission
from The New York Times Magazine

00:22:01.295 --> 00:22:03.414
to write about depression
among the indigent.

00:22:03.438 --> 00:22:04.675
And I turned in my story,

00:22:04.699 --> 00:22:08.159
and my editor called me and said,
"We really can't publish this."

00:22:08.668 --> 00:22:09.827
And I said, "Why not?"

00:22:09.851 --> 00:22:11.922
And she said, "It just is too far-fetched.

00:22:11.946 --> 00:22:15.609
These people who are sort of
at the very bottom rung of society

00:22:15.633 --> 00:22:17.648
and then they get
a few months of treatment

00:22:17.672 --> 00:22:20.045
and they're virtually ready
to run Morgan Stanley?

00:22:20.069 --> 00:22:21.585
It's just too implausible."

00:22:22.013 --> 00:22:24.594
She said, "I've never even heard
of anything like it."

00:22:24.618 --> 00:22:27.071
And I said, "The fact
that you've never heard of it

00:22:27.095 --> 00:22:29.198
is an indication that it is news."

00:22:29.907 --> 00:22:33.930
(Laughter)